   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8f2d6a01",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# SPA: Búsqueda de hiperparámetros\n",
    "\n",
    "Este notebook se ejecuta en local porque el cómputo gratuito de Databricks era limitado para lanzar cientos de entrenamientos. Lee gold_split.csv, exportado desde 11_challenger, que marca cada cliente como train o test con el mismo split que se usó para el champion. Solo se usa la parte de train. La regresión logística base reproduce en local la PR-AUC que dio en Databricks, lo que confirma que el montaje es correcto. Random forest, gradient boosting y XGBoost se ajustaron con búsqueda aleatoria o en rejilla y validación cruzada de 5 folds. Los tres quedan empatados en ~0.674, a ~0.02 de la regresión logística, en el límite de lo que consideramos ruido. Los tres modelos de árboles eligieron una profundidad máxima de 2, lo que indica que la relación con el churn es casi aditiva y que el límite lo ponen los datos más que el algoritmo. Los hiperparámetros elegidos se entrenan y comparan con el champion en 11_challenger."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "16dfd8e7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ENG: Hyperparameter search\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook runs locally, because the free Databricks compute was limited for launching hundreds of training runs. It reads gold_split.csv, exported from 11_challenger, which marks each customer as train or test using the same split as the champion. Only the train part is used. The baseline logistic regression reproduces locally the PR-AUC it obtained in Databricks, which confirms the setup is correct. Random forest, gradient boosting and XGBoost were tuned with random or grid search and 5-fold cross-validation. All three tie at ~0.674, ~0.02 above logistic regression, at the limit of what we consider noise. All three tree models chose a maximum depth of 2, which indicates that the relationship with churn is almost additive and that the limit is set by the data more than by the algorithm. The selected hyperparameters are trained and compared with the champion in 11_challenger."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 0,
   "metadata": {
    "application/vnd.databricks.v1+cell": {
     "cellMetadata": {},
     "inputWidgets": {},
     "nuid": "ab4aef1a-3eb1-4844-8e3f-6f00083a1c38",
     "showTitle": false,
     "tableResultSettingsMap": {},
     "title": ""
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, \"..\")\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import GradientBoostingClassifier, RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import RandomizedSearchCV, StratifiedKFold, cross_val_score\n",
    "from xgboost import XGBClassifier\n",
    "\n",
    "from churn.config import ID, TARGET, RANDOM_SEED\n",
    "from churn.pipeline import construir_pipeline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 0,
   "metadata": {
    "application/vnd.databricks.v1+cell": {
     "cellMetadata": {},
     "inputWidgets": {},
     "nuid": "218d1212-5905-4b8d-9012-0e90d2a953b1",
     "showTitle": false,
     "tableResultSettingsMap": {},
     "title": ""
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pdf = pd.read_csv(\"../data/gold_split.csv\")\n",
    "train = pdf[pdf[\"conjunto\"] == \"train\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train = train.drop(columns=[ID, TARGET, \"conjunto\"])\n",
    "y_train = train[TARGET]\n",
    "\n",
    "cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=RANDOM_SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "assert len(train) == 5634, f\"{len(train)} filas de train\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 0,
   "metadata": {
    "application/vnd.databricks.v1+cell": {
     "cellMetadata": {},
     "inputWidgets": {},
     "nuid": "efd3139b-9175-4b8b-a81d-bbe70e0ad08b",
     "showTitle": false,
     "tableResultSettingsMap": {},
     "title": ""
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "logreg = construir_pipeline(LogisticRegression(random_state=RANDOM_SEED))\n",
    "scores = cross_val_score(logreg, X_train, y_train, cv=cv, scoring=\"average_precision\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 0,
   "metadata": {
    "application/vnd.databricks.v1+cell": {
     "cellMetadata": {},
     "inputWidgets": {},
     "nuid": "7fa42c76-83fb-439a-b0c2-cee37d2eff58",
     "showTitle": false,
     "tableResultSettingsMap": {},
     "title": ""
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(scores.mean())\n",
    "print(scores.std())"
   ]
  },
